  "rationale": "CS-R1 (csharp review): bare-identifier value reads \u2014 the analyzer emitted none at all while the oracle audits only calls/instantiates (CONV-CS-1, same both-sides-blind class as pre-review CP1/R1). Every bare identifier naming a class member VALUE (fields, consts, properties) is a Uses edge: static/instance reads (Get), shadowing suppression (Shadowed param), pattern bindings (is-pattern p, switch-arm q, colliders p/q/x/y/v/w/a/b deliberately collide with members so reverts leak), lambda params + query vars (Flow, with post-binding LIMIT/Max reads proving no over-suppression), out-var and deconstruction bindings (Guards), designators that never read (with/subpattern/anontype/attribute-named), nameof/typeof silence (NameOf), setter-`value` skip with getter member read (WithProps), inheritance + nested-class reads (Shared), member/enumerator initializers (Holder/Level), top-level calls to global (CS-B1), file-scoped types private + unexported (CS-B4), catch_clause complexity on both catch forms (CS-B3).",
